CORE
outside.c
--function f --pointer-check
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[precondition_instance\.1\] .*static array parameter x must provide access to its declared minimum: SUCCESS$
^\[f\.pointer_dereference\.\d+\] line 3 dereference failure: pointer outside object bounds in x\[\(signed long int\)n\]: FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The --function harness provides exactly the runtime static minimum, so an
access one element past it still fails the ordinary pointer check.
